// DISABLED — see the note in app/surveys/page.tsx.
//
// A route-level loading.tsx turns the page into a streamed Suspense boundary.
// With this file present, Next emitted its streaming placeholders
// (<template id="P:…">) INSIDE the property-type <select>. The HTML parser
// discards anything that is not an <option> inside a <select>, so those
// placeholders never existed in the DOM, every $RS() call that targeted one
// threw "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'parentNode')", and hydration
// for the WHOLE route died — React never attached and the form rendered as
// inert HTML. Nothing in the markup was invalid; the placeholders simply landed
// somewhere the parser refuses to keep them.
//
// Restore only alongside a fix that keeps boundaries out of <select> — e.g.
// rendering the long option lists from a client component.
